<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="041" project="email-communication-intelligence-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Attachment-grounded action extraction — ground the Action on extracted attachment text (text-extraction → SPE → child-`sprk_document`), deterministically gated to action-triggers, cited to attachment + locator</title>
    <phase>P4 — Job C + intent</phase>
    <gate>after:040</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <tags>bff-api, catalog</tags>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Highest-difficulty AI in r1 (spec / plan §8) — extracting an action stated only in an attachment and citing it to the exact attachment locator. Heaviest eval-case obligation (NFR-07). Grounds a create on the Job C path (040), so the deadline→confirm + citation-verification obligations carry through. Deterministically gated to likely action-triggers for cost. BFF-touching: publish-size + CVE + Placement Justification; code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The hardest extraction problem in the project — action buried in attachment PDF text, cited precisely to attachment + locator, with a deterministic cost gate; reasoning quality on extraction accuracy + citation fidelity is decisive.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P4</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Grounds on 040's create-task path + shares `Services/Communication/` + `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`; serialize after 040. `/conflict-check` before the PR.</parallel-reason>
    <dependencies>040</dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement **attachment-grounded action extraction** (FR-13): the triage/action Action grounds on **extracted attachment text** (via the existing text-extraction → SPE → child-`sprk_document` pipeline) and extracts an action stated **only in an attachment**, **deterministically gated to likely action-triggers** (for cost), and **cited to the attachment + locator**. The extracted action feeds the Job C create path (040).

    Reach AI **only** through `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` (ADR-013 facade) as a **code-directed Action + Binding** (ADR-039). MUST NOT land capability on the frozen node-graph engine. Reuse the existing attachment text-extraction pipeline (SPE → child-`sprk_document`) — do NOT build a new extractor. Reuse the Job C create path (040) for the resulting task/event — do NOT fork a second create mechanism.

    **Cost gate (NFR-08-style discipline):** run the LLM extraction ONLY on attachments that a **deterministic pre-filter** flags as likely action-triggers (do not extract from every attachment). **Citation fidelity (NFR-06):** the extracted action MUST be cited to the attachment + a precise locator, and the cited text MUST be verified to exist in the extracted attachment text before proposing/creating; deadline-bearing entries require confirm (ADR-015). **NFR-04:** best-effort / non-fatal on the enrichment path.

    This is the **highest-difficulty AI** in r1 — the **heaviest golden-utterance eval-case obligation** (NFR-07): the eval must demonstrate extraction of an action present ONLY in an attachment, cited to the attachment.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication + Ai domains, authoritative on the attachment text-extraction pipeline (text-extraction → SPE → child-`sprk_document`), the `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` facade (ADR-013), Action + Binding authoring (ADR-039), the Job C create path (040), NFR-06 citation verification, NFR-07 eval obligation, and cost-gating discipline.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Given an email with an attachment whose text (extracted via the existing SPE → child-`sprk_document` pipeline) states an action not present in the body, a deterministic pre-filter flags it as a likely action-trigger, the Action extracts the action cited to the attachment + locator (verified to exist), and it feeds the Job C create path (040) with deadline-bearing entries gated to confirm. Extraction runs only on flagged attachments (cost). A golden-utterance eval case demonstrates the attachment-only extraction + citation. Best-effort on the enrichment path. Build clean; unit + seam tests + the eval case pass; publish-size + CVE + Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Some obligations/actions live only in an attachment (a PDF "please execute by Aug 15"), not the email body. FR-13 extracts those. The attachment text is already available via the existing pipeline (text-extraction → SPE → child-`sprk_document`) — this task grounds the Action on that extracted text, it does NOT build a new extractor. The resulting action feeds the Job C create path (040), so 040's citation + deadline→confirm obligations carry through, now cited to the attachment + locator.

      This is the hardest AI problem in r1 (plan §8): the action is buried in document text and the citation must point precisely at the attachment span. To control cost, a deterministic pre-filter gates which attachments get an LLM extraction pass (do not extract from all). NFR-07: the eval-case obligation is heaviest here — the golden utterance must have the action ONLY in the attachment.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IActionSeam.cs (REUSE — facade seam; extraction Action + the create it feeds go through here)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Nodes/ActionCore/TaskActionCore.cs (REUSE via 040 — the create path the extracted action feeds)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationEnrichmentService.cs (REFERENCE — enrichment path; extraction fires best-effort + cost-gated, NFR-04)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/AiClassificationRung.cs (REFERENCE — the triage signal / action-trigger context)</file>
      <file>infra/dataverse/inputschemas/create-task-v1.input.schema.json (REUSE via 040 — the create the extracted action targets)</file>
      <file>docs/guides/ai-guide-consumer-wiring.md (Action + Binding authoring; RAG/attachment grounding)</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/tasks/040-job-c-email-triggered-work-create-task.poml (the create path this grounds on)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>040 (the Job C create path the extracted action feeds).</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-13">Scope: ground the triage/action Action on extracted attachment text (existing text-extraction → SPE → child-`sprk_document`), deterministically gated to likely action-triggers; an action stated only in an attachment is extracted and cited to the attachment + locator.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Scope: code-directed Action + Binding via catalog data; MUST NOT land capability on the frozen node-graph engine; reuse the existing attachment extraction pipeline (no new extractor) + the Job C create path (no forked create).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-03">Scope: reach AI ONLY via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`; MUST NOT inject `IOpenAiClient`/`IPlaybookService` into Communication code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06 / ADR-015">Scope: the extracted action is cited to the attachment + a precise locator; the system verifies the cited text exists in the extracted attachment text before proposing/creating; deadline-bearing entries require confirm; nothing deadline-bearing auto-finalizes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08 / cost">Scope: run the LLM extraction ONLY on attachments a deterministic pre-filter flags as likely action-triggers; do NOT extract from every attachment; report the gating behavior.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04 / ADR-045">Scope: extraction is best-effort / non-fatal — it MUST NOT fail the capture or send / enrichment path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-07 / ADR-039">Scope: heaviest eval obligation — a golden-utterance eval case MUST demonstrate extraction of an action present ONLY in an attachment, cited to the attachment (blocking merge gate).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §10">Scope: BFF Hygiene — load `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; state Placement Justification (grounds on existing extraction + Job C path via PublicContracts; catalog data, no new service); publish-size delta vs ~49.63 MB (expected ≈0); no new HIGH CVE; update tests + seam tests.</constraint>
  </constraints>

