    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Ground on extracted attachment text" location="child-sprk_document (SPE text-extraction)">
        Read the already-extracted attachment text (text-extraction → SPE → child-`sprk_document`); ground the extraction Action on it; do NOT build a new extractor.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Deterministic cost gate" location="Services/Communication/CommunicationEnrichmentService.cs">
        A deterministic pre-filter flags likely action-trigger attachments; run the LLM extraction only on flagged attachments; the rest are skipped (cost).
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Attachment-locator citation" location="Services/Ai/PublicContracts/">
        Cite the extracted action to the attachment + a precise locator; verify the cited span exists in the extracted text before feeding the create path (NFR-06).
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`, `docs/guides/ai-guide-consumer-wiring.md` (attachment/RAG grounding), ADR-039, ADR-013, ADR-015, and 040's create-path decisions.</step>
    <step order="2">Read the attachment extraction pipeline (text-extraction → SPE → child-`sprk_document`), `IActionSeam.cs`, and the enrichment path — identify where extracted attachment text is available + where the trigger fires best-effort.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement the deterministic action-trigger pre-filter (which attachments get an LLM extraction pass) — cost gate; report the gating behavior.</step>
    <step order="4">Author the extraction Action + Binding (catalog data) grounded on the extracted attachment text that produces an action + a citation to the attachment + a precise locator; verify the cited span exists in the extracted text before proceeding (NFR-06).</step>
    <step order="5">Feed the extracted action into the Job C create path (040): create the task/event cited to the attachment; deadline-bearing entries require confirm (ADR-015). Reuse 040's create path — no forked create.</step>
    <step order="6">Wire best-effort onto the enrichment path (NFR-04) — log + degrade on failure, never throw up capture/send.</step>
    <step order="7">Add the golden-utterance eval case (NFR-07, heaviest): an action present ONLY in an attachment is extracted + cited to the attachment. Write unit + seam tests: (a) attachment-only action extracted + cited to attachment + locator; (b) NEGATIVE — an attachment NOT flagged by the pre-filter is not LLM-extracted (cost gate); (c) NEGATIVE — an extracted action whose cited text is not in the attachment is not created (citation verification); (d) deadline-bearing → confirm; (e) extraction failure does not fail the enrichment path (NFR-04). ADR-038 boundary mocks only.</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + targeted `dotnet test`; publish-size (report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB) + CVE scan.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor gates: `code-review` (focus reuse-of-extractor + Job C create, cost gate, citation fidelity, facade discipline, non-fatal); `adr-check` against ADR-039 / ADR-013 / ADR-015 + spec FR-13 / NFR-04 / NFR-06 / NFR-07. Address Critical findings; cite Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/`; coordinate with 040 on the create path).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (041 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (pre-filter design, attachment-text grounding point, locator-citation approach, eval case).</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the existing attachment text-extraction pipeline does not expose extracted text at the granularity needed to produce a precise attachment locator (so citation fidelity cannot be met without a new extractor), STOP and surface per root §6 / §6.5 rather than building a parallel extraction pipeline.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The text-extraction → SPE → child-`sprk_document` pipeline already extracts attachment text; the Job C create path (040) already creates cited tasks/events; the classification/triage signal (022) provides action-trigger context.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — this is a new Action + Binding (catalog data) + a deterministic pre-filter, grounding on the existing extracted text + feeding the existing create path; no new extractor, no new create mechanism, no new service.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without attachment-grounded extraction, an action stated only in an attachment (a PDF deadline) is invisible to triage — the obligation is missed (FR-13 / Success Criterion 7 fails), the highest-value email-intelligence differentiator.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="read">Inspect the extraction pipeline, facade seam, Job C create path, enrichment path, wiring guide</tool>
    <tool name="grep">Confirm reuse of the extractor + Job C create (no new extractor / forked create); confirm facade discipline</tool>
    <tool name="edit">Implement the pre-filter + extraction Action/Binding + create wiring</tool>
    <tool name="bash">Build, unit/seam tests, eval-case render, publish-size, CVE scan</tool>
    <tool name="code-review">FULL-rigor gate (Step 9.5)</tool>
    <tool name="adr-check">FULL-rigor gate (Step 9.5)</tool>
    <tool name="conflict-check">Pre-PR hot-path scan (Step 10)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/ + Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ (UPDATED — deterministic action-trigger pre-filter + attachment-grounded extraction Action feeding the Job C create path, cited to attachment + locator, best-effort)</output>
    <output type="config">infra/dataverse/ (extraction Action + Binding rows; heaviest golden-utterance eval case — attachment-only action)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ + tests/integration/seam/ — attachment-only-extracted-cited + cost-gate-skips-unflagged + citation-verified + deadline→confirm + non-fatal</output>
    <output type="docs">PR description with §11 Component Justification + bff-extensions Placement Justification + publish-size delta + CVE result</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">An action stated ONLY in an attachment PDF is extracted and cited to the attachment + a precise locator, and feeds the Job C create path (040).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The LLM extraction runs ONLY on attachments a deterministic pre-filter flags as likely action-triggers; unflagged attachments are not extracted (cost gate, verifiable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: an extracted action whose cited text is not present in the extracted attachment text is not created (citation verification, NFR-06); deadline-bearing entries require confirm.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reuses the existing extraction pipeline + the Job C create path — no new extractor, no forked create (grep-verifiable); AI reached only via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`; no frozen-engine landing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Extraction is best-effort: a failure does NOT fail the capture or send / enrichment path (NFR-04).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The heaviest golden-utterance eval case (action ONLY in an attachment, cited to the attachment) exists and passes (NFR-07).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; tests pass; publish-size delta ≈0 vs ~49.63 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Highest-difficulty AI in r1 (plan §8) with the heaviest eval obligation. Grounds on the existing extraction pipeline + the Job C create path (040) — reuse, do not rebuild. The deterministic cost gate + attachment-locator citation fidelity are the two decisive properties. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/`).
  </notes>

